            <ArticleTitle>[Probable stenocardial effects of combined oral contraceptives].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>3123-30</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>One case of myocardial infarction and one case of coronary insufficiency, observed in women treated with oral contraceptives, are presented. Pathogenetic hypotheses are put forward and stress is laid on the necessity of evaluating risk factors as well as carrying out the various hemogenic tests in these patients.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
